==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
Germanic ''*drepan'' (to strike, push, beat), Indo-European ''*dhrebh-, *dhreb-'' (to crack, crush, kill); cf Old English ''[[drepan]]'', German ''[[treffen]]'' (hit, meet).

===Verb===
'''drepa''', [[drep]]; [[drap]], [[drápum]]; [[drepinn]]

# to [[beat]], to [[hit]], to [[push]], to [[knock]]
# to [[kill]], to [[slay]]
# to [[capture]] (''e.g. in chess'')

====Descendants====
